<title>USA: ICF Kaiser says gets work order of $45 mln.</title>
<headline>ICF Kaiser says gets work order of $45 mln.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFAX, Va. 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>ICF Kaiser International Inc said Friday it has negotiated new work assignments, worth more than $45 million with the U.S. Army.</p>
<p>ICF said the assignments were for cleaning up two sites, one in Baltimore, Md. and Sacramento, Calif, under the Total Environmental Remediation Contract it has with the army.</p>
<p>The sites, ICF says, are filled with hazardous waste that it will clean and help convert into usable areas for civilians.</p>
</text>
